# ---------------------------------------------------------------- redaction table
# The real identifier table is never committed. A public repo must not contain
# the strings it exists to hide, and `git log` would keep them forever.
# See SANITISATION.md. Example shape: redactions.example.txt
redactions.local.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- captured secrets
# Signed streaming-CDN URLs embed a device fingerprint and per-session signatures.
*cast-log.txt
*.local.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- captured device data
# Raw, unsigned captures — scrubbed copies live in evidence/
loot/
baseline/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build artefacts
build/
*.zip
*.bplist.tmp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run output
status.txt
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- third-party disclosure material
# Kept out of the repo while a coordinated disclosure is open.
hardening/
SUBMISSION.md
CERT-coordination-request.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
node_modules/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- keychain material
# The sideload tool stores the developer password in the macOS login keychain.
# Nothing of it should ever have a plaintext form on disk.
*.keychain
*.keychain-db
dev-password*
